    "name": "rapideye",
    "title": "RapidEye - Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF",
    "description": "RapidEye product over Brazil. Launched on August 29, 2008, the RapidEye constellation consisted of five identical medium-resolution satellites, each carrying the REIS sensor. This collection provides orthorectified images with 5‑meter spatial resolution. The constellation was officially decommissioned on December 31, 2019, and no longer acquires new imagery. Brazil obtained RapidEye images for the years 2011-2015, covering the entire national territory. The data is available in Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF format, with 5-meter spatial resolution and a temporal resolution of 5 days. The collection includes the following spectral bands: Blue (B01), Green (B02), Red (B03), Red Edge (B04), and Near Infrared (B05).",
